                <pb facs="0958" n="860" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg860"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Peirce.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-11-14"><hi rendition="#italic">November 14,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>[Mr. Hay approves the protocol transmitted with Mr. Peirce’s No. 139, except that
                    the “<hi rendition="#italic">Cape Horn Pigeon</hi>” should be described as
                    having been engaged in whaling instead of sealing.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
